[{:db/id 17592186064354 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d61e161d-c16f-54c4-b847-5ce2fd8181a2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186063965 :question/problem "What is the value of $-6 + 9?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $9$ to $-6,$ we start at $-6$ on a number line and move $9$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/f3/f3fc6c865056b9a177ab65d7a4477102c3e0d28035a14230bdf8c630c262e270.png)\n\nWe end up at $3.$ So, $-6+9=3.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-6+9 = 9-6 = 3\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064355 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b19e586f-b5e5-54ad-9f34-9f32c29b74be" "question-456bbb28-9f6e-59b4-94a9-4565fc858899" "question-dbe692b7-3891-54fa-af44-56909b7f8af6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186063966 :question/problem "What is $-3.5 + 6.5?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064356 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-04148a8c-1c50-5c75-a5ce-265853c3b05d" "question-2f37489a-3f1a-5d45-bf2c-50769e7aa76a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186063967 :question/problem "Find the value of $-\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{5}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We put both fractions over a common denominator of $6$ and then add the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{5}{3} = -\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{10}{6} = \\dfrac{-7+10}{6}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $10$ to $-7,$ we start at $-7$ on a number line and move $10$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/6f/6fc38c489951a4c0f26a5ff0ddc3da199da9ac71a2afc396701f8999921cb4a6.png)\n\nSo, $-7 + 10 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{-7 + 10}{6} = \\dfrac{3}{6} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{-7 + 10}{6} = \\dfrac{10 - 7}{6} = \\dfrac{3}{6} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{5}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-d61e161d-c16f-54c4-b847-5ce2fd8181a2" :question/id #uuid "d61e161d-c16f-54c4-b847-5ce2fd8181a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-2111" :question/problem "$-2+4=$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $4$ to $-2,$ we start at $-2$ on a number line and move $4$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/29/291bb445c414ae60c0093038554a780370b3e4d747e7e51a737aa15ffa7a6cf0.png)\n\nWe end up at $2.$ So, $-2+4=2.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-2+4=4-2=2\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a262c79-dfba-55a4-a56d-f3ec1cfd98f4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a262c79-dfba-55a4-a56d-f3ec1cfd98f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a262c79-dfba-55a4-a56d-f3ec1cfd98f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-84427d74-3ee1-560e-bc68-770067d24981" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f6a526c1-f065-5fe2-8d96-7ea86354ca6c" "answer-39bdbb7d-1c2e-52f0-adb2-575085e56b8c" "answer-84427d74-3ee1-560e-bc68-770067d24981" "answer-23598180-5131-56ac-a678-284f1be0f865" "answer-029931bb-b5f8-5fb0-9873-fecc74600828"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6a526c1-f065-5fe2-8d96-7ea86354ca6c" :answer/id #uuid "f6a526c1-f065-5fe2-8d96-7ea86354ca6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39bdbb7d-1c2e-52f0-adb2-575085e56b8c" :answer/id #uuid "39bdbb7d-1c2e-52f0-adb2-575085e56b8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84427d74-3ee1-560e-bc68-770067d24981" :answer/id #uuid "84427d74-3ee1-560e-bc68-770067d24981" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23598180-5131-56ac-a678-284f1be0f865" :answer/id #uuid "23598180-5131-56ac-a678-284f1be0f865" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-029931bb-b5f8-5fb0-9873-fecc74600828" :answer/id #uuid "029931bb-b5f8-5fb0-9873-fecc74600828" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064555 :question/problem "$-5+6=$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $6$ to $-5,$ we start at $-5$ on a number line and move $6$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/a3/a33a6894112c333711ee25f2bb79abd458448d5c0d4131ddbc53f4f828cc161e.png)\n\nWe end up at $1.$ So, $-5+6=1.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-5+6=6-5=1\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186061525 :answer-field/correct 17592186061528 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-b19e586f-b5e5-54ad-9f34-9f32c29b74be" :question/id #uuid "b19e586f-b5e5-54ad-9f34-9f32c29b74be" :question/math-academy-id "q-171019" :question/problem "$-5.1+7.8=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-5.1+7.8=7.8-5.1=2.7\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-063dade4-c614-5849-9dd5-3fd50b05fb88"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-063dade4-c614-5849-9dd5-3fd50b05fb88" :answer-field/id #uuid "063dade4-c614-5849-9dd5-3fd50b05fb88" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fa1dfaf1-bfb2-5467-8046-aad5191102e4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa1dfaf1-bfb2-5467-8046-aad5191102e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa1dfaf1-bfb2-5467-8046-aad5191102e4" :answer/id #uuid "fa1dfaf1-bfb2-5467-8046-aad5191102e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-456bbb28-9f6e-59b4-94a9-4565fc858899" :question/id #uuid "456bbb28-9f6e-59b4-94a9-4565fc858899" :question/math-academy-id "q-186761" :question/problem "$-4+1.3=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-4+1.3=1.3-4=-2.7\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce961bdb-0b16-58aa-9186-57cb2f2ecbd3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce961bdb-0b16-58aa-9186-57cb2f2ecbd3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce961bdb-0b16-58aa-9186-57cb2f2ecbd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d8c29228-4935-5f4f-92c0-8084c40f90c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8c29228-4935-5f4f-92c0-8084c40f90c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8c29228-4935-5f4f-92c0-8084c40f90c1" :answer/id #uuid "d8c29228-4935-5f4f-92c0-8084c40f90c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dbe692b7-3891-54fa-af44-56909b7f8af6" :question/id #uuid "dbe692b7-3891-54fa-af44-56909b7f8af6" :question/math-academy-id "q-186759" :question/problem "$-7.2+9=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-7.2+9=9-7.2=1.8\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7e5b8b97-ae6f-5b9d-81bd-9420bb384ac9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7e5b8b97-ae6f-5b9d-81bd-9420bb384ac9" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e5b8b97-ae6f-5b9d-81bd-9420bb384ac9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4cd19208-d390-5649-bac1-18dae3a47955" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4cd19208-d390-5649-bac1-18dae3a47955"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cd19208-d390-5649-bac1-18dae3a47955" :answer/id #uuid "4cd19208-d390-5649-bac1-18dae3a47955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-04148a8c-1c50-5c75-a5ce-265853c3b05d" :question/id #uuid "04148a8c-1c50-5c75-a5ce-265853c3b05d" :question/math-academy-id "q-186817" :question/problem "$-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We put both fractions over a common denominator of $15$ and then add the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{9}{15}=\\frac{-7+9}{15}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $9$ to $-7,$ we start at $-7$ on a number line and move $9$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/f2/f2d170548e38956afa1354e7df74f645ea5101c3dde6665c110ada01ab7a96b8.png)\n\nSo, $-7+9=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+9}{15}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+9}{15}=\\frac{9-7}{15}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{2}{15}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2d674a5c-fdfd-5d98-b059-a94b119773c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2d674a5c-fdfd-5d98-b059-a94b119773c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d674a5c-fdfd-5d98-b059-a94b119773c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6964b9d9-786b-5c01-9b32-664218330975" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6964b9d9-786b-5c01-9b32-664218330975"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6964b9d9-786b-5c01-9b32-664218330975" :answer/id #uuid "6964b9d9-786b-5c01-9b32-664218330975" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f37489a-3f1a-5d45-bf2c-50769e7aa76a" :question/id #uuid "2f37489a-3f1a-5d45-bf2c-50769e7aa76a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42771" :question/problem "$-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions have a common denominator of $6$, we can combine them to form one fraction, which gives\n \n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{-1+5}{6}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $5$ to $-1,$ we start at $-1$ on a number line and move $5$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/63/632e4bcce5b619f9a5c4dfb2c414a33da0e9567b7b4d8b15adb439da1b3dd88d.png)\n\nSo, $-1+5=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-1+5}{6}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1+5}{6}=\\frac{5-1}{6}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54f6bfc9-156f-56af-9a68-93e35ceaafd4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54f6bfc9-156f-56af-9a68-93e35ceaafd4" :answer-field/id #uuid "54f6bfc9-156f-56af-9a68-93e35ceaafd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef3643e8-e01d-5c50-898f-0a065ba5fe4b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2da51ed-49ab-5a35-8936-978067b61077" "answer-f221eb0f-a3ec-559c-96de-9b221d2f6830" "answer-fe1d4d2c-65a3-5028-a3c4-6fec7489e8ab" "answer-1bb6d7c8-0f9b-5a72-997d-9319e4d9909f" "answer-ef3643e8-e01d-5c50-898f-0a065ba5fe4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2da51ed-49ab-5a35-8936-978067b61077" :answer/id #uuid "d2da51ed-49ab-5a35-8936-978067b61077" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f221eb0f-a3ec-559c-96de-9b221d2f6830" :answer/id #uuid "f221eb0f-a3ec-559c-96de-9b221d2f6830" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe1d4d2c-65a3-5028-a3c4-6fec7489e8ab" :answer/id #uuid "fe1d4d2c-65a3-5028-a3c4-6fec7489e8ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bb6d7c8-0f9b-5a72-997d-9319e4d9909f" :answer/id #uuid "1bb6d7c8-0f9b-5a72-997d-9319e4d9909f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef3643e8-e01d-5c50-898f-0a065ba5fe4b" :answer/id #uuid "ef3643e8-e01d-5c50-898f-0a065ba5fe4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065430 :tutorial/content "There are two ways to add a positive number to a negative number. Let's work out the value of $-5+7$ using both methods.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nWhen we add, we move to the right on the number line.\n\nSo, to add $7$ to $-5,$ we start at $-5$ on a number line and move $7$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/e6/e6f99b09208d09824dc7c4e6dfaafdc0e20feb7fde00f821a57a70d79196936d.png)\n\n \n\nWhen we do this, we land at $2.$ Therefore, $-5+7 =2.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nAdding a positive number to a negative number is like *subtraction in reverse*. To turn the addition into a subtraction, we must switch the numbers around.\n\nSo, to work out ${\\color{red}{-5}} + {\\color{blue}{7}},$ we can switch the numbers around to get \n$\\,{\\color{blue}{7}} {\\color{red}{\\,-\\,5}} =2.$\n\nWe're allowed to swap the numbers because addition is **commutative**, which means the order in which we add two numbers does not matter." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065431 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we want to calculate $-\\dfrac 1 3 + \\dfrac 5 3.$\n\nSince both fractions have a common denominator of $3,$ we can combine them to form one fraction:\n\n \n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{1}{3} + \\dfrac{5}{3} =\\dfrac{-1+5}{3}\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either method that we've learned.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $5$ to $-1,$ we start at $-1$ on a number line and move $5$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/63/632e4bcce5b619f9a5c4dfb2c414a33da0e9567b7b4d8b15adb439da1b3dd88d.png)\n\nWe end up at $4.$ So $-1+5=4,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{-1+5}{3} = \\dfrac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1+5}{3}=\\frac{5-1}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\dfrac1 3 + \\dfrac 5 3 = \\dfrac{4}{3}.$\n\n**Note:** If two fractions have different denominators, we need to put them over a common denominator *first* and *then* subtract!" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064420 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
